      "vae_summary": {
        "input_id": "input_001",
        "title": "Variational Autoencoder Formulation",
        "concepts_and_definitions": [
          "Variational Autoencoder (VAE)",
          "Evidence Lower Bound (ELBO)",
          "Reconstruction loss (log\u2011likelihood term)",
          "Kullback\u2011Leibler (KL) divergence between approximate posterior and prior",
          "Reparameterization trick for stochastic gradient descent",
          "Latent variable z with mean \u03bc and variance \u03c3\u00b2"
        ],
        "mechanisms_and_formulas": [
          "L(\u03b8,\u03c6;x)=E_{q_\u03c6(z|x)}[log\u202fp_\u03b8(x|z)]\u2212D_{KL}(q_\u03c6(z|x)\u2016p(z))",
          "z=\u03bc+\u03c3\u00b7\u03b5 \u2003with\u2003\u03b5\u223c\ud835\udca9(0,I) (reparameterization)",
          "D_{KL}(\ud835\udca9(\u03bc,\u03c3\u00b2)\u2016\ud835\udca9(0,I))=\u2212\u00bd\u2211_{i}(1+log\u202f\u03c3_i\u00b2\u2212\u03bc_i\u00b2\u2212\u03c3_i\u00b2)"
        ],
        "examples_and_code_patterns": [
          "TensorFlow reparameterization:\u202fz = mu + tf.exp(0.5 * log_var) * eps",
          "ELBO loss computation in TF/Keras:\nrecon_loss = tf.reduce_sum(tf.keras.losses.binary_crossentropy(x, x_decoded), axis=[1,2,3])\nkl_loss = -0.5 * tf.reduce_sum(1 + log_var - tf.square(mu) - tf.exp(log_var), axis=1)\nloss = tf.reduce_mean(recon_loss + kl_loss)"
        ],
        "factual_summary_text": "The material introduces the Variational Autoencoder (VAE) as a generative model that learns a probabilistic mapping between data x and latent variables z. Training maximizes the Evidence Lower Bound (ELBO), which consists of two terms: a reconstruction loss that encourages the decoder p_\u03b8(x|z) to reproduce the input, and a KL\u2011divergence term that regularizes the approximate posterior q_\u03c6(z|x) toward a chosen prior p(z), typically a standard normal distribution. The ELBO is expressed as L(\u03b8,\u03c6;x)=E_{q(z|x)}[log\u202fp(x|z)]\u2212D_{KL}(q(z|x)\u2016p(z)).\n\nTo enable gradient\u2011based optimization despite the stochastic sampling of z, the reparameterization trick is employed: a sample z is obtained by shifting and scaling a noise variable \u03b5 drawn from a fixed distribution, usually \u03b5\u223c\ud835\udca9(0,I), using the encoder\u2019s predicted mean \u03bc and variance \u03c3\u00b2 (or log\u2011variance log_var). In TensorFlow this appears as z = mu + tf.exp(0.5 * log_var) * eps. The KL term for Gaussian q and p has a closed\u2011form expression, allowing efficient computation of the ELBO loss during training."
      }
